{
  "id": "mxgchkd",
  "title": "CHAPTER 2: OPERATING SYSTEMS",
  "order": 2,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "zamgx97",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Introduction and Functions of OS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Operating Systems oversee system resources through core modules: Process, Memory, File, and I/O Management.",
        "Process Management includes thread allocation, state transitions, and execution scheduling using CPU Scheduling Algorithms.",
        "Process Synchronisation deals with concurrent execution risks, resolving the Critical Section Problem and preventing Deadlocks.",
        "Memory Management optimizes RAM utilization using Page Replacement Algorithms.",
        "I/O Systems and Disk Scheduling organize external storage access and minimize read/write seek time."
      ],
      "id": "999i4ke"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Core Modules",
          "value": "6 Units",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Concept",
          "value": "Process & Memory",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Concurrency Control",
          "value": "Synchronisation & Deadlock",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Storage Handling",
          "value": "Disk Scheduling",
          "icon": "clock"
        }
      ],
      "id": "47z2mgs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3j19s2o",
      "content": "An Operating System (OS) is system software that manages computer hardware, software resources, and provides services for computer programs. It acts as an intermediary between users and hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "xgtn9vm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Functions of OS"
    },
    {
      "id": "x6acciv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Process Management — create, schedule, synchronise, terminate processes",
        "Memory Management — allocate/deallocate memory; virtual memory; paging; segmentation",
        "File System Management — organise, store, retrieve, protect files and directories",
        "Device Management — manage I/O devices through device drivers; interrupt handling",
        "Security and Protection — user authentication; access control; isolation between processes",
        "Networking — manage network protocols, sockets, communication"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1mb6n7w",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>OS Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Batch OS</p>",
            "<p>Jobs collected and processed without user interaction; high throughput</p>",
            "<p>Early IBM systems, Payroll processing</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Time-Sharing OS</p>",
            "<p>Multiple users share CPU time; quick response; context switching</p>",
            "<p>Unix, Linux, Windows Server</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Real-Time OS (RTOS)</p>",
            "<p>Strict timing constraints; deterministic; hard/soft real-time</p>",
            "<p>VxWorks, FreeRTOS, embedded systems, medical devices</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Distributed OS</p>",
            "<p>Multiple computers work as single system; transparent to user</p>",
            "<p>Amoeba, Plan 9, cloud OS platforms</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Network OS</p>",
            "<p>Manages resources on a network; file/print sharing</p>",
            "<p>Windows Server, Novell NetWare</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mobile OS</p>",
            "<p>Designed for mobile devices; touch interface; power-efficient</p>",
            "<p>Android, iOS, HarmonyOS</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Embedded OS</p>",
            "<p>Designed for specific hardware; resource-constrained</p>",
            "<p>RTOS variants, Linux for routers, Arduino OS</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "glxwqv4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.2 Process Management"
    },
    {
      "id": "czdh00r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Process vs Thread"
    },
    {
      "id": "j6o43jh",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Aspect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Process</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Thread</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Definition</p>",
            "<p>Program in execution; independent</p>",
            "<p>Lightweight unit within process; shares process resources</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Memory</p>",
            "<p>Own memory space (code, data, heap, stack)</p>",
            "<p>Shares code, data, heap; own stack and registers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Creation overhead</p>",
            "<p>High (fork/exec system calls)</p>",
            "<p>Low (thread creation much faster)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Communication</p>",
            "<p>IPC (pipes, sockets, shared memory)</p>",
            "<p>Direct through shared memory within process</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Context switch</p>",
            "<p>Expensive</p>",
            "<p>Cheaper (less state to save)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Crash impact</p>",
            "<p>Does not affect other processes</p>",
            "<p>Can crash entire process</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Example</p>",
            "<p>Chrome: each tab is a process</p>",
            "<p>Web server: each request is a thread</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rk9cfd0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Process States"
    },
    {
      "id": "9uf6h5d",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "New: process being created",
        "Ready: waiting to be assigned CPU",
        "Running: currently executing on CPU",
        "Waiting/Blocked: waiting for I/O or event",
        "Terminated: process has finished execution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ebvr26f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "CPU Scheduling Algorithms"
    },
    {
      "id": "xxrn99q",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Algorithm</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Preemptive?</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Metric</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Limitation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>FCFS (First Come First Served)</p>",
            "<p>Non-preemptive</p>",
            "<p>No</p>",
            "<p>Simple; no starvation</p>",
            "<p>Convoy effect; poor avg waiting time</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SJF (Shortest Job First)</p>",
            "<p>Non-preemptive</p>",
            "<p>No</p>",
            "<p>Optimal avg waiting time</p>",
            "<p>Requires knowing burst time in advance; starvation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SRTF (Shortest Remaining Time First)</p>",
            "<p>Preemptive SJF</p>",
            "<p>Yes</p>",
            "<p>Optimal preemptive</p>",
            "<p>Starvation of long jobs; overhead</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Round Robin (RR)</p>",
            "<p>Preemptive</p>",
            "<p>Yes</p>",
            "<p>Fair; time quantum q</p>",
            "<p>High context switch overhead if q too small</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Priority Scheduling</p>",
            "<p>Both versions</p>",
            "<p>Both</p>",
            "<p>Urgent tasks run first</p>",
            "<p>Starvation of low-priority; aging solution</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Multilevel Queue</p>",
            "<p>Non-preemptive</p>",
            "<p>Varies</p>",
            "<p>System/interactive/batch separation</p>",
            "<p>Rigid; inter-queue starvation possible</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Multilevel Feedback Queue</p>",
            "<p>Preemptive</p>",
            "<p>Yes</p>",
            "<p>Adaptive; most practical OS use this</p>",
            "<p>Most complex to configure</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8y9hsn9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.3 Process Synchronisation"
    },
    {
      "id": "6gauc6x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Critical Section Problem"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ogqz5x",
      "content": "A critical section is a code segment that accesses shared resources and must not be executed by more than one process simultaneously. Requirements for a solution: Mutual Exclusion, Progress, Bounded Waiting."
    },
    {
      "id": "16l69rj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Synchronisation Mechanisms"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Attribute",
        "Process",
        "Thread"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Definition",
          "An independent execution unit with its own memory space",
          "A lightweight segment of a process executing tasks concurrently"
        ],
        [
          "Memory & Resources",
          "Allocated separate memory and address space",
          "Shares memory and address space with the parent process"
        ],
        [
          "Context Switching",
          "Slower context switching due to isolated address space",
          "Faster context switching due to shared resources"
        ],
        [
          "Termination Impact",
          "Termination does not directly terminate other processes",
          "Termination of parent process terminates all its threads"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "mp2ds0w"
    },
    {
      "id": "do65hii",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Mechanism</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example Use</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mutex (Mutual Exclusion Lock)</p>",
            "<p>Binary lock; only owner can release; prevents concurrent access</p>",
            "<p>Protecting a shared variable or data structure</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Semaphore</p>",
            "<p>Integer variable; P (wait/down) and V (signal/up) operations</p>",
            "<p>Producer-consumer, reader-writer, dining philosophers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Binary Semaphore</p>",
            "<p>Semaphore with value 0 or 1; equivalent to mutex</p>",
            "<p>Simple mutual exclusion</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Counting Semaphore</p>",
            "<p>Value can be any non-negative integer</p>",
            "<p>Managing finite pool of resources (e.g., connection pool)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Monitor</p>",
            "<p>High-level synchronisation; encapsulates shared data + procedures</p>",
            "<p>Java synchronized methods, condition variables</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Spinlock</p>",
            "<p>Busy-waiting lock; process loops until lock available</p>",
            "<p>Short critical sections in multiprocessor systems</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Condition Variable</p>",
            "<p>Allows thread to wait until condition holds; used with mutex</p>",
            "<p>Producer-consumer with empty/full conditions</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "98kaqzy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Deadlock"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ihcbyu",
      "content": "Deadlock is a situation where a set of processes are permanently blocked, each waiting for a resource held by another process in the set."
    },
    {
      "id": "td27a18",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Coffman Condition</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Prevention Strategy</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mutual Exclusion</p>",
            "<p>Resource held by exactly one process at a time</p>",
            "<p>Make resources shareable (not always possible)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hold and Wait</p>",
            "<p>Process holds resources while waiting for more</p>",
            "<p>Request all resources at once (pre-allocation)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>No Preemption</p>",
            "<p>Resources cannot be forcibly taken; must be voluntarily released</p>",
            "<p>Allow preemption (take resources away if needed)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Circular Wait</p>",
            "<p>Circular chain of processes waiting for each other</p>",
            "<p>Impose total ordering of resource types; always request in order</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hheiq4p",
      "content": "<strong>Note: </strong><em>All 4 Coffman conditions must hold simultaneously for deadlock to occur. Breaking any one prevents deadlock. Banker's Algorithm is used for deadlock avoidance.</em>"
    },
    {
      "id": "lmb4in9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.4 Memory Management"
    },
    {
      "id": "1y0r4se",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Contiguous Allocation</p>",
            "<p>Process gets one block of memory; external fragmentation issue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Paging</p>",
            "<p>Fixed-size pages (process) mapped to frames (physical memory); eliminates external fragmentation; page table needed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Segmentation</p>",
            "<p>Variable-size segments (logical view — code, data, stack); external fragmentation possible</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Virtual Memory</p>",
            "<p>Allows execution of processes not completely in RAM; enables larger address space than physical RAM</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Demand Paging</p>",
            "<p>Pages loaded only when needed; page fault triggers loading from disk</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Page Replacement Algorithms</p>",
            "<p>FIFO, Optimal, LRU, LRU Approximation (Clock/Second Chance), LFU</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Thrashing</p>",
            "<p>Excessive paging; process spends more time swapping pages than executing; caused by too many processes in memory</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Translation Lookaside Buffer (TLB)</p>",
            "<p>Fast cache for page table entries; reduces memory access time; associative memory</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Internal Fragmentation</p>",
            "<p>Wasted space inside allocated block (paging)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>External Fragmentation</p>",
            "<p>Free memory scattered in small pieces; can't satisfy large request (contiguous)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0xtwd5y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Page Replacement Algorithms"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "CPU Scheduling Algorithms (FCFS, SJF, Round Robin, Priority) are frequently tested for calculating average waiting and turnaround times.",
        "Deadlock conditions (Mutual Exclusion, Hold and Wait, No Preemption, Circular Wait) and Banker's Algorithm are high-yield exam topics.",
        "Page Replacement Algorithms (FIFO, LRU, Optimal) and Belady's Anomaly are recurring questions in competitive exams.",
        "Disk Scheduling algorithms (SSTF, SCAN, C-SCAN, LOOK) are consistently evaluated for head movement calculation."
      ],
      "id": "prcavnd"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a9e0jg",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Algorithm</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Strategy</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Belady's Anomaly?</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Notes</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>FIFO</p>",
            "<p>Replace page that has been in memory longest</p>",
            "<p>Yes (more frames can increase faults)</p>",
            "<p>Simple; poor performance</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Optimal (OPT)</p>",
            "<p>Replace page that won't be used for longest time</p>",
            "<p>No</p>",
            "<p>Impossible in practice; used as benchmark</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LRU</p>",
            "<p>Replace least recently used page</p>",
            "<p>No</p>",
            "<p>Good performance; costly implementation; stack/counter based</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Clock (Second Chance)</p>",
            "<p>FIFO + reference bit; give second chance if recently used</p>",
            "<p>Yes</p>",
            "<p>Practical approximation of LRU; used in Linux</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>LFU</p>",
            "<p>Replace least frequently used page</p>",
            "<p>No</p>",
            "<p>Requires frequency counters; aging technique used</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r01guua",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.5 File Systems"
    },
